117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Aspiring athletes, particularly students and young players from rural areas and economically disadvantaged backgrounds, often lack access to professional coaches and scientific sports assessment facilities. As a result, many talented individuals remain undiscovered due to limited opportunities to demonstrate their abilities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Existing sports talent assessment methods often rely on manual observation and subjective judgments, leading to inconsistent evaluations. The high cost of professional assessment and the lack of standardized testing make it difficult to compare athletes fairly and identify their strengths and weaknesses.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Therefore, there is a need for an affordable, accessible, and reliable system that enables standardized and transparent sports talent assessment. Addressing this gap can help identify promising athletes, provide equal opportunities, and support talent development regardless of geographical location or financial background.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
